From: well0nez <8986239+well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] hid: h713-remote: the BLE remote's focus keys are the other way round

0169 mapped the consumer usages 0x0de and 0x0df of the stock BLE remote to
KEY_F4 (focus up) and KEY_F5 (focus down). Over infrared the same two keys
arrive through the rc keymap of 0254 (0x0251 -> KEY_F4, 0x0250 -> KEY_F5),
and that direction is right: measured on the HY310 with the owner at the
wall (16.10.2026, the focus moves the way the key says). Over Bluetooth the
keys did the opposite: with a fresh bond on 18.10.2026 the owner pressed
"focus up" and the motor ran down, and "focus down" ran it up; the overlay
showed the direction the motor actually ran. So 0x0de is the down key and
0x0df the up key. The remote's key names were never read from a document;
the infrared table is the one confirmed at the wall.

Signed-off-by: well0nez <8986239+well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/hid/hid-h713-remote.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/hid/hid-h713-remote.c b/drivers/hid/hid-h713-remote.c
--- a/drivers/hid/hid-h713-remote.c
+++ b/drivers/hid/hid-h713-remote.c
@@ -59,8 +59,8 @@ static int h713_remote_input_mapping(struct hid_device *hdev, struct hid_input *hi,
 		return 1;
 	case 0x0de:
-		hid_map_usage_clear(hi, usage, bit, max, EV_KEY, KEY_F4);
+		hid_map_usage_clear(hi, usage, bit, max, EV_KEY, KEY_F5);
 		return 1;
 	case 0x0df:
-		hid_map_usage_clear(hi, usage, bit, max, EV_KEY, KEY_F5);
+		hid_map_usage_clear(hi, usage, bit, max, EV_KEY, KEY_F4);
 		return 1;
 	}
